allSemistandardTableaux -- list all semistandard Young tableaux of a given shape
********************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        allSemistandardTableaux(lam,mu,N)
        allSemistandardTableaux L
  * Inputs:
      * lam, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the outer shape, $\lambda$.
      * mu, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the inner shape, $\mu$.
      * N, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the maximum entry.
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of tuples
        ($\lambda^{(i)}$,$\mu^{(i)}$,$N^{(i)}$).
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note bag: (Macaulay2Doc)Bag,, bagged list of all SSYT of given
        shape and entries in 1..N. If N is not provided, it is assumed to be
        the length of the shape.

Description
===========

The resulting bag can be thought of as the set $\mathrm{SSYT}(\lambda,\mu,N)$
of semistandard Young tableaux of shape $\lambda/\mu$ and entries in
$1,2,\ldots,N$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
