positionList -- get the positions of all the boxes in a tableau
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        positionList T
        positionList(T,f)
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, a
        tableau.
      * f, a *note function: (Macaulay2Doc)Function,, a function that acts on
        the positions, and returns either true or false.
  * Outputs:
      * l, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the positions (i,j) of boxes in
        T. If a function f is provided, then only the positions returning true
        are in the list.

Description
===========

This method is useful for iterating over all positions in a tableau.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = youngTableau(new Partition from {6,3,2}, new Partition from {2},    |
|                                                                             |
|               ┌────┬────┬────┬────┐                                         |
|o1 =           │ 10 │ 11 │ 12 │ 13 │                                         |
|     ┌────┬────┼────┼────┴────┴────┘                                         |
|     │ 14 │ 15 │ 16 │                                                        |
|     ├────┼────┼────┘                                                        |
|     │ 17 │ 18 │                                                             |
|     └────┴────┘                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : YoungTableau                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|toList(10..18))                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : theList = positionList T                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = {(0, 2), (0, 3), (0, 4), (0, 5), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (2, 0), (2, 1)}|
|                                                                             |
|o2 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T' = youngTableau(new Partition from {6,3,2}, new Partition from {2},   |
|                                                                             |
|                       ┌────────┬────────┬────────┬────────┐                 |
|o3 =                   │ (0, 2) │ (0, 3) │ (0, 4) │ (0, 5) │                 |
|     ┌────────┬────────┼────────┼────────┴────────┴────────┘                 |
|     │ (1, 0) │ (1, 1) │ (1, 2) │                                            |
|     ├────────┼────────┼────────┘                                            |
|     │ (2, 0) │ (2, 1) │                                                     |
|     └────────┴────────┘                                                     |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : YoungTableau                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|theList)                                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Including a function returns only the positions that return true. For example,
the following code returns all positions of corners in the tableau, using
function *note isCorner: isCorner,.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : positionList(T, thePosition -> isCorner(thePosition,T))|
|                                                            |
|o4 = {(0, 5), (1, 2), (2, 1)}                               |
|                                                            |
|o4 : List                                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note toPosition: toPosition, -- get the position of a box, given its index
  * *note toIndex: toIndex, -- get the index of a box, given its position

Ways to use positionList:
=========================

  * "positionList(YoungTableau)"
  * "positionList(YoungTableau,Function)"

For the programmer
==================

