skewShape -- the shape of a skew tableau
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        (lam,mu) = skewShape T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, a skew
        tableau.
  * Outputs:
      * lam, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the outer shape, $\lambda$, of T.
      * mu, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the inner shape, $\mu$, of T.

Description
===========

This returns the original shape used to construct the tableau.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = youngTableau(new Partition from {4,3,1,0}, new Partition from {2,1},|
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───┬───┐                                                       |
|o1 =         │ 1 │ 2 │                                                       |
|         ┌───┼───┼───┘                                                       |
|         │ 3 │ 4 │                                                           |
|     ┌───┼───┴───┘                                                           |
|     │ 5 │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : YoungTableau                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{1,2,3,4,5})                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : skewShape T                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = (Partition{4, 3, 1, 0}, Partition{2, 1})                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

It may be convenient to remove trailing $0$'s from the partitions by using trim
on a sequence of two partitions.

+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : trim skewShape T                     |
|                                          |
|o3 = (Partition{4, 3, 1}, Partition{2, 1})|
|                                          |
|o3 : Sequence                             |
+------------------------------------------+

It may also be useful to append $0$s to make the partitions have the same
number of parts.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (lam',mu') = pad skewShape T                            |
|                                                             |
|o4 = (Partition{4, 3, 1, 0}, Partition{2, 1, 0, 0})          |
|                                                             |
|o4 : Sequence                                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : rowLengths' = for i from 0 to #lam'-1 list(lam'#i-mu'#i)|
|                                                             |
|o5 = {2, 2, 1, 0}                                            |
|                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

You may also 'standardize' a skew shape to return a pair of partitions of equal
length, without extra $0$'s. I.e., one of the resulting partitions will end
with a nonzero part, and the other will be padded with $0$'s.

+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : (lam'',mu'') = standardize skewShape T                    |
|                                                               |
|o6 = (Partition{4, 3, 1}, Partition{2, 1, 0})                  |
|                                                               |
|o6 : Sequence                                                  |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : rowLengths = for i from 0 to #lam''-1 list(lam''#i-mu''#i)|
|                                                               |
|o7 = {2, 2, 1}                                                 |
|                                                               |
|o7 : List                                                      |
+---------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note shape: shape, -- the shape of a Young tableau
  * *note standardize: standardize, -- standardize the lengths of a pair of
    partitions

