File: Tableaux.info, Node: standardize, Next: Tabloid, Prev: skewShape, Up: Top

standardize -- standardize the lengths of a pair of partitions
**************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (lam',mu') = standardize (lam,mu)
  * Inputs:
      * lam, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        a partition.
      * mu, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        a partition.
  * Outputs:
      * lam', an instance of the type *note Partition:
        (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,, a partition obtained from lam, with trailing
        zeros added or removed.
      * mu', an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        a partition obtained from mu, with trailing zeros added or removed.
  * Consequences:
      * Partitions lam' and mu' have the same number of parts, possibly with
        trailing 0s.

Description
===========

A tableau T of shape $\lambda/\mu$ may be constructed with
$\ell(\lambda)\neq\ell(\mu)$. It is common to iterate over the rows of T, and
it is convenient to append trailing 0s to the shorter partition. This method
effectively removes all trailing 0s from both shapes, then appends 0s to the
shorter shape until they have the same length.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = youngTableau(new Partition from {4,3,1,0}, new Partition from {2,1})|
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───┬───┐                                                       |
|o1 =         │   │   │                                                       |
|         ┌───┼───┼───┘                                                       |
|         │   │   │                                                           |
|     ┌───┼───┴───┘                                                           |
|     │   │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : YoungTableau                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : skewShape T                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = (Partition{4, 3, 1, 0}, Partition{2, 1})                                |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : standardize skewShape T                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = (Partition{4, 3, 1}, Partition{2, 1, 0})                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Sequence                                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note skewShape: skewShape, -- the shape of a skew tableau
  * *note shape: shape, -- the shape of a Young tableau

Ways to use standardize:
========================

  * "standardize(Partition,Partition)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note standardize: standardize, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

