File: Tableaux.info, Node: tabloid, Next: Tabloid == Tabloid, Prev: Tabloid, Up: Top

tabloid -- constructor for type Tabloid
***************************************

  * Usage: 
        tabloid(lam, mu, entryList)
        tabloid((lam,mu),entryList)
  * Inputs:
      * lam, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the outer shape $\lambda$.
      * mu, an instance of the type *note Partition: (Macaulay2Doc)Partition,,
        the inner shape $\mu$. If not given, then it is assumed to be the $0$
        partition.
      * entryList, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, the filling of the boxes.
  * Outputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note Tabloid: Tabloid,, a tabloid of shape
        $\lambda/\mu$ with the given filling.
  * Consequences:
      * The list of entries has length equal to
        $\sum_{i=1}^{\ell(\lambda)}|\lambda_i-\mu_i|$. E.g., if $\lambda=(2)$
        and $\mu=(5)$, then the entry list must have length $3$.
      * The entries are $\{1,\ldots,N\}$, where $N$ is the number of boxes.

Description
===========

+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : lam = new Partition from {4,3,2}|
|                                     |
|o1 = Partition{4, 3, 2}              |
|                                     |
|o1 : Partition                       |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : mu = new Partition from {3,1}   |
|                                     |
|o2 = Partition{3, 1}                 |
|                                     |
|o2 : Partition                       |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : entryList = {1,4,2,3,5}         |
|                                     |
|o3 = {1, 4, 2, 3, 5}                 |
|                                     |
|o3 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : T = tabloid(lam,mu,entryList)   |
|                                     |
|                 ┌───┐               |
|o4 =             │ 1 │               |
|         ┌───────┼───┘               |
|         │ 4   2 │                   |
|     ┌───┴───┬───┘                   |
|     │ 3   5 │                       |
|     └───────┘                       |
|                                     |
|o4 : Tabloid                         |
+-------------------------------------+

See also
========

  * *note Tabloid: Tabloid, -- a type of HashTable representing a Young tabloid
  * *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau, -- a type of HashTable representing a
    Young tableau

Ways to use tabloid:
