Tabloid == Tabloid -- check if two tabloids are equal
*****************************************************

  * Operator: *note ==: (Macaulay2Doc)==,
  * Usage: 
        T1 == T2
  * Inputs:
      * T1, an instance of the type *note Tabloid: Tabloid,, a tabloid.
      * T2, an instance of the type *note Tabloid: Tabloid,, a tabloid.
  * Outputs:
      * b, a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the tabloids
        are equal or not.

Description
===========

Two tabloids are equal if they have the same representative. That is, if their
corresponding rows contain the same numbers.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T1 = tabloid(new Partition from {5,3,1}, new Partition from {2},        |
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───────────┐                                                   |
|o1 =         │ 7   2   4 │                                                   |
|     ┌───────┴───┬───────┘                                                   |
|     │ 1   3   6 │                                                           |
|     ├───┬───────┘                                                           |
|     │ 5 │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : Tabloid                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{7,2,4,1,3,6,5})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : T2 = tabloid(new Partition from {5,3,1}, new Partition from {2},        |
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───────────┐                                                   |
|o2 =         │ 2   7   4 │                                                   |
|     ┌───────┴───┬───────┘                                                   |
|     │ 3   6   1 │                                                           |
|     ├───┬───────┘                                                           |
|     │ 5 │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : Tabloid                                                                 |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{2,7,4,3,6,1,5})                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T1 == T2                                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o3 = true                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note Tabloid == Tabloid: Tabloid == Tabloid, -- check if two tabloids are
    equal
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

