tex(YoungTableau) -- LaTeX output for a tableau
***********************************************

  * Function: *note tex: (Macaulay2Doc)tex,
  * Usage: 
        tex T
  * Inputs:
      * T, an instance of the type *note YoungTableau: YoungTableau,, a
        tableau.
  * Outputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, the LaTeX code for
        reproducting the given tableau.

Description
===========

The LaTeX code uses commands from the LaTeX package aTableau (see
https://github.com/AndrewMathas/aTableau ).

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = youngTableau(new Partition from {4,3,1}, new Partition from {2,1},  |
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───┬───┐                                                       |
|o1 =         │ 1 │ 2 │                                                       |
|         ┌───┼───┼───┘                                                       |
|         │ 3 │ 4 │                                                           |
|     ┌───┼───┴───┘                                                           |
|     │ 5 │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o1 : YoungTableau                                                            |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|{1,2,3,4,5})                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : tex T                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = \SkewTableau[skew border, skew boxes]{2, 1, 0}{12, 34, 5}               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : T' = tabloid T                                                          |
|                                                                             |
|             ┌───────┐                                                       |
|o3 =         │ 1   2 │                                                       |
|         ┌───┴───┬───┘                                                       |
|         │ 3   4 │                                                           |
|     ┌───┼───────┘                                                           |
|     │ 5 │                                                                   |
|     └───┘                                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Tabloid                                                                 |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : tex T'                                                                  |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = \Tabloid[skew={2, 1, 0}]{12, 34, 5}                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

